<style>
  :root {
    --font-family: "<%= (session && session.fontStyle ? String(session.fontStyle).trim() : 'Inter') %>", sans-serif;
    --primary: #01535b;
    --primary-light: #e8f4f5;
    --border: #e5e7eb;
    --text: #1f2937;
    --text-muted: #6b7280;
    --bg: #f9fafb;
  }

  body {
    font-family: var(--font-family);
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0;
    background-color: var(--bg);
    line-height: 1.7;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }

  main {
    max-width: 1140px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .page-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }

  .page-header p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legal-section {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 28px 28px 24px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .section-num {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--primary-light);
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .legal-section p {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-section ul {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .legal-section li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .legal-section li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 8px;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--primary);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .contact-card {
    background: var(--primary-light);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .contact-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .contact-card a {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .contact-card a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    main { padding: 100px 0 40px; }
    .page-header { margin: 20px 12px 40px; }
    .page-header h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
    .legal-section { margin: 0 12px 20px; padding: 20px 18px; }
    .contact-card { margin: 0 12px; padding: 10px 10px 28px; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    main { padding: 110px 0 32px; }
    .page-header { margin: 30px 8px 40px; }
    .page-header h1 { font-size: 1.35rem; }
    .page-header p { font-size: 0.88rem; }
    .legal-section { margin: 0 8px 20px; padding: 16px 14px; border-radius: 10px; }
    .legal-section h2 { font-size: 1.02rem; }
    .legal-section p { font-size: 0.92rem; }
    .legal-section li { font-size: 0.9rem; padding-left: 20px; }
    .section-num { width: 24px; height: 24px; font-size: 0.78rem; }
    .contact-card { margin: 0 8px; padding: 16px 16px 28px; border-radius: 10px; }
    .contact-card p { font-size: 0.9rem; }
  }
</style>

</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <div class="page-header">
      <h1>Managira Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>Last Updated: November 15, 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <p>Managira is a student information system for K-12 schools and school districts in the United States, operated by ScREAte ("Managira," "we," "us"). This Privacy Policy explains what information Managira collects, how we use and protect it, and the commitments we make to the schools, families, and students who rely on us.</p>
      <p>Student information deserves the highest level of care. Schools own and control the student data they place in Managira. We use it only to provide the service the school has chosen, we never sell it, and we never use it for advertising.</p>
      <p>Where a school or district has signed a separate agreement with Managira, such as a data privacy agreement or a state-specific addendum, that agreement governs if it conflicts with this Privacy Policy.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2><span class="section-num">1</span> Scope and Our Role</h2>
      <p>This Privacy Policy covers information processed through Managira's websites, web and mobile applications, school dashboards, parent and student portals, integrations, and support channels.</p>
      <p>When a school, district, or group of schools ("School") uses Managira, the School decides what information is collected and how it is used. Managira processes that information on the School's behalf and under its direction, as a service provider. For information collected on our own public websites, such as a request for a demonstration, Managira is responsible for that information as described in this policy.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2><span class="section-num">2</span> Information We Collect</h2>
      <p><strong>Student data.</strong> Information about students that a School or its authorized users enter into Managira, such as name, student number, date of birth, grade level and class, enrollment and attendance records, grades, assessments, report cards, transcripts, schedules, transportation details, guardian relationships, emergency and pickup contacts, photos, and forms the School asks families or students to complete.</p>
      <p><strong>Account information.</strong> Names, email addresses, phone numbers, roles, and sign-in details for school staff, parents and guardians, and students who are given access by their School.</p>
      <p><strong>Billing information.</strong> Information needed to manage a School's subscription and, where a School uses Managira to collect fees, the details needed to process those payments. Card and bank details are handled by our payment processor and are not stored by Managira.</p>
      <p><strong>Technical information.</strong> IP addresses, browser and device details, sign-in events, and activity logs needed to operate the service, keep accounts secure, and investigate problems.</p>
      <p><strong>Communications.</strong> Messages sent to our support team and information provided when someone requests a demonstration or contacts us.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2><span class="section-num">3</span> How We Use Information</h2>
      <p>We use information to provide, secure, support, and maintain Managira for the School that uses it. That includes creating and managing accounts, running the features the School has turned on, generating the reports and documents the School requests, sending messages on the School's behalf, processing payments, answering support requests, preventing misuse, and meeting our legal obligations.</p>
      <p>We may use de-identified or aggregated information, from which no student, family, or School can be identified, to understand how the service performs and to improve it. We do not attempt to re-identify such information and we contractually prohibit anyone we share it with from doing so.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section" id="student-data">
      <h2><span class="section-num">4</span> Our Student Data Commitments</h2>
      <p>For all student data, Managira commits to the following:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not sell student data or any personal information.</li>
        <li>We do not use student data for targeted advertising, and we do not show advertising to students based on their information or activity.</li>
        <li>We do not build profiles of students except as needed for the educational purposes the School directs.</li>
        <li>We do not use student data to develop or train artificial intelligence models for use outside the School's own service.</li>
        <li>We collect and keep only the student data needed to provide the service.</li>
        <li>The School retains ownership and control of its student data and can export it at any time.</li>
        <li>We disclose student data only to the School and its authorized users, to service providers bound by written obligations at least as protective as this policy, or when required by law.</li>
        <li>We will not make material changes to how we use student data without first notifying the School and, where the law requires, obtaining consent.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section" id="ferpa">
      <h2><span class="section-num">5</span> FERPA</h2>
      <p>When Managira provides services to a School subject to the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA), Managira acts as a "school official" with a legitimate educational interest under 34 C.F.R. &sect; 99.31(a)(1). The School keeps direct control over our use and maintenance of education records.</p>
      <p>We use personally identifiable information from education records only to provide the services the School has requested, and we do not re-disclose it except as the School directs or as FERPA allows. Requests from parents or eligible students to inspect, review, or correct education records are handled by the School. Managira helps the School respond promptly and within the time the law requires.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section" id="coppa">
      <h2><span class="section-num">6</span> COPPA and Children Under 13</h2>
      <p>Managira does not knowingly collect personal information directly from children under 13 except at the direction of their School. As permitted by the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and Federal Trade Commission guidance, a School may consent on behalf of parents to the collection of a child's information when it is used solely for an educational purpose and for no other commercial purpose. Managira relies on that School authorization and uses such information only to provide the service to the School.</p>
      <p>Parents may ask their child's School to review the information collected about their child, to have it deleted, or to stop further collection. Managira will assist the School in carrying out those requests. If we learn that we have collected information from a child under 13 without appropriate authorization, we will delete it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section" id="state-laws">
      <h2><span class="section-num">7</span> State Student Privacy Laws and Data Privacy Agreements</h2>
      <p>Managira is designed to support Schools in meeting state student privacy laws, including the California Student Online Personal Information Protection Act (SOPIPA) and California Education Code &sect; 49073.1, New York Education Law &sect; 2-d and Part 121 of the Regulations of the Commissioner of Education, the Illinois Student Online Personal Protection Act (SOPPA), and comparable laws in other states.</p>
      <p>We sign the Student Data Privacy Consortium National Data Privacy Agreement and state-specific data privacy agreements and addenda on request. Where an agreement requires more of us than this policy does, we follow the agreement.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2><span class="section-num">8</span> How We Share Information</h2>
      <p>We share information only in the following circumstances:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>With the School and its authorized users</strong>, according to the roles and permissions the School assigns.</li>
        <li><strong>With service providers</strong> that host, secure, and operate the service on our behalf, such as cloud hosting, file storage, email and text message delivery, and payment processing. Each is bound by a written agreement to use the information only to provide its service to us and to protect it. The current list is published at <a href="/legal/subprocessors">managira.com/legal/subprocessors</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>With integrations a School or user turns on</strong>, such as Google Classroom or a calendar connection, limited to what that feature requires.</li>
        <li><strong>With people a School chooses to send a Gov/state report to</strong>, such as its state or district education agency. The file is never attached to an email: each person gets a secure link that works for 7 days and a one-time code in a separate email, and every send and download is recorded for the School.</li>
        <li><strong>When required by law</strong>, such as to respond to a valid subpoena or court order. Unless prohibited, we notify the School before disclosing its data so it can respond.</li>
        <li><strong>In a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets</strong>, only to a successor that agrees to honor the commitments in this policy for previously collected student data.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section" id="google-microsoft-data">
      <h2><span class="section-num">9</span> Google and Microsoft Account Data</h2>
      <p>Some Managira features connect to a Google or Microsoft account. Managira receives only the access a person approves on Google's or Microsoft's own consent screen, and uses it only for the feature that person or their school turned on:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Classroom</strong> (connected by a school): Managira creates and updates Classroom courses for the school's own classes, keeps each course's teachers and students the same as the school's enrollment in Managira (matching people by email address), posts the school's assessments as assignments and keeps grades the same in both places after a teacher approves them, and, only if the school turns it on, invites students' parents or guardians as Classroom guardians.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Calendar and Microsoft Outlook</strong> (connected by a person for themselves): Managira creates one calendar named "Managira" in that person's account and adds, updates and removes in it what their Managira calendar shows them: events, tasks, classes, and the coming weeks' birthdays they can see (names only, never ages). Managira does not read, change or delete any of their other calendars or events.</li>
        <li><strong>The account's email address</strong>, to show which Google or Microsoft account is connected.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Access tokens are stored encrypted and are used only to provide these features. Disconnecting in Managira removes the Managira calendar and Managira's stored access, and a person can also remove Managira's access at any time from their Google Account (Security, Third-party apps) or Microsoft account settings.</p>
      <p>Managira does not sell Google or Microsoft user data, does not use it for advertising, and does not use it to develop, improve or train generalized artificial intelligence or machine learning models. People at Managira do not read it unless the account owner asks us to (for example for support), it is needed for security, or the law requires it.</p>
      <p>Managira's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" style="color:var(--primary);font-weight:600;">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section" id="data-location">
      <h2><span class="section-num">10</span> Where Data Is Stored</h2>
      <p>Managira stores student data, including student records and the photos and files Schools and families upload, with hosting providers in the United States. We do not transfer student data to be stored outside the United States.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section" id="security">
      <h2><span class="section-num">11</span> How We Protect Information</h2>
      <p>Managira maintains administrative, technical, and physical safeguards appropriate to the sensitivity of student data, aligned with recognized frameworks such as the NIST Cybersecurity Framework. Our safeguards include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Encryption.</strong> All connections to Managira use HTTPS, and browsers are instructed to use only secure connections. Databases, backups, and stored files are encrypted at rest. Credentials for connected services are encrypted with AES-256-GCM.</li>
        <li><strong>Access control.</strong> Schools assign each user a role and specific permissions, and every request is checked against them on our servers. Staff can grant others no more access than they hold themselves.</li>
        <li><strong>Sign-in protection.</strong> Passwords are stored only as salted bcrypt hashes. Password sign-ins are confirmed with a one-time code, sent by email or shown by an authenticator app (which a School can require for its staff), and passwords found in known data breaches are refused, repeated failed attempts are slowed, and sessions end after a period set by the School. Schools can require sign-in through their own identity provider using SAML or OpenID Connect, including that provider's multi-factor authentication.</li>
        <li><strong>Private files.</strong> Student photos and uploaded documents are kept in private storage and are shown only to signed-in users of the School they belong to, through links that expire within minutes.</li>
        <li><strong>Monitoring and logging.</strong> Sign-ins, permission changes, and other significant actions are recorded in activity logs available to School administrators.</li>
        <li><strong>Backups and recovery.</strong> Production databases are backed up continuously, allowing recovery to a recent point in time, and backups are encrypted.</li>
        <li><strong>Secure development.</strong> Code changes pass automated tests before release, dependencies are checked for known vulnerabilities on every change and weekly, and the service is regularly tested for security weaknesses, including attempts to reach one school&rsquo;s data from another.</li>
        <li><strong>Limited internal access.</strong> Access to customer data by Managira personnel is limited to those who need it to support and secure the service. Personnel with access are bound by confidentiality obligations, and their access is removed when it is no longer needed.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>No system can be made completely secure, but we work continuously to protect the information entrusted to us and to improve our safeguards.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section" id="breach-notification">
      <h2><span class="section-num">12</span> Security Incidents and Breach Notification</h2>
      <p>Managira maintains a written incident response plan. If we confirm that student data or other personal information was accessed or acquired without authorization, we will notify the affected School without unreasonable delay and no later than 72 hours after confirmation, unless a law enforcement agency asks us to delay. Where a School's agreement or state law requires a shorter period, we meet that requirement.</p>
      <p>Our notice will describe, to the extent known, what happened and when, the types of information involved, the steps we have taken to contain the incident and protect the information, and a contact for questions. We will cooperate with the School's investigation, support it in notifying affected parents, students, and staff as the law requires, and take reasonable steps to prevent a recurrence.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section" id="retention">
      <h2><span class="section-num">13</span> Data Retention, Return, and Deletion</h2>
      <p>We keep student data only as long as needed to provide the service to the School, or as the School directs. A School can export its data at any time.</p>
      <p>When a School's agreement ends, or when a School asks in writing, we delete its student data from our active systems within 60 days, after giving the School the opportunity to export it. Copies in encrypted backups are deleted as those backups expire in the normal course. We confirm deletion in writing on request. We may keep information that the law requires us to retain, and de-identified information as described in Section 3.</p>
      <p>Account and billing records relating to a School's subscription are kept as needed to meet our legal, tax, and accounting obligations.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2><span class="section-num">14</span> Access, Correction, and Other Requests</h2>
      <p>Parents, guardians, and eligible students who want to review, correct, or delete student information should contact their School, which controls those records. Managira will help the School respond.</p>
      <p>Other individuals may contact us using the details below to ask about, correct, or delete personal information that Managira holds about them. We may need to verify a person's identity before acting on a request, and we will respond within the time the applicable law requires.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2><span class="section-num">15</span> Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
      <p>Managira uses cookies and similar technologies that are needed to keep users signed in, protect accounts, remember preferences, and keep the service working. We do not use advertising or cross-site tracking cookies in the signed-in application or the parent and student portals.</p>
      <p>Most browsers let users control cookies, but blocking the cookies Managira needs will prevent users from signing in.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2><span class="section-num">16</span> Communications</h2>
      <p>We send service messages that are needed to operate Managira, such as sign-in codes, security notices, billing notices, and messages a School sends through Managira. We may send product news to School administrators and other business contacts, who can unsubscribe at any time. We never use student data to market to students or families.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2><span class="section-num">17</span> Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy as our service or the law changes. We will post the updated policy with a new date. Before making a material change to how we collect or use student data, we will notify Schools at least 30 days in advance, and the change will not apply to student data collected earlier without the School's consent.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2><span class="section-num">18</span> Contact Us</h2>
      <p>Questions about this Privacy Policy, requests concerning personal information, and reports of a suspected security issue may be sent to:</p>
      <p>Managira (ScREAte)<br>Email: <a href="mailto:info@managira.com" style="color:var(--primary);font-weight:600;">info@managira.com</a></p>
      <p>Schools with a signed data privacy agreement may also use the contacts named in that agreement.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>